 ## Changelog
 
+- 2026-10-25 (5): animals graze, root, peck and rest, and every walk has its own gait (**NOT b1.7.3**, same switch as the smart animals of (4); written WITHOUT a Rust toolchain: not compiled, not run; +4 tests `mobs::tests::{a_cow_grazes_still_head_down_and_stops_for_a_visitor_or_a_blow, each_kind_has_its_own_pause, a_resting_animal_stays_put_and_does_not_turn, walks_have_their_own_gait_and_only_hens_dash}`, +1 `items::tests::a_grazing_head_dips_to_the_ground_not_through_it`; run `cargo test --lib mobs items` first). Pig, cow, sheep and chicken only; the wolf, squid and every monster are untouched. b1.7.3 has none of this: its animals only stand, turn and wander.
+    - `Mob::idle` (new): what a calm smart animal does with a pause, called when a walk ends (3 in 4 it eats if the ground allows, `arrived`) and 1 tick in 70 while it stands (1 in 4). Cow and sheep graze on grass (60..160 ticks), a pig roots on grass or dirt (40..100), a hen pecks on any solid ground (15..40); when it does not eat, 1 pause in 8 of a cow, sheep or pig is a rest (160..400 ticks). Nothing starts with a person within 4 blocks.
+    - While `graze` or `rest` runs (`Mob::roam` counts it down at 20 Hz) the animal picks no walk, does not turn (`ai_walk` clears `look` / `yaw_vel`) and stands. A person within 4 blocks, or a blow (`Mob::damage`, which also starts the panic of (4)), ends it at once.
+    - Gait: `pick_dest` gives each walk `gait` = 0.6..1.0 x `moveSpeed`, a hen 1 walk in 4 is a 1.5 x dash; `ai_walk` uses it for wander walks only (panic is still 1.5 x, a chase or a tame wolf's walk is untouched).
+    - Drawing: `Mob::head` (0 up .. 1 down, eased by 0.8 a tick in `Mob::step`) and `Mob::munch` (a phase that runs while the head is down: 0.3 a tick, a hen 0.9). `render/items.rs::head_dip` turns the head box (and a hen's beak) about its own pivot by 1.1 rad (cow, sheep), 0.6 (pig) or 0.9 (hen) x `head`, with a +-0.08 rad chew or a quick hen peck from `munch`, and moves the pivot down so the nose touches the ground (`GROUND`, model y 23.875) and never goes through it.
+    - Compatibility: `Mob::smart` is false until `Mobs::herd` sets it, and every new branch is behind it or behind `graze` / `rest` / `wander`, which only a smart animal sets; `animalAi:false` draws the same random numbers as before.
+    - ponytail: the grass is not eaten (no block write from `Mobs`; sheep do not regrow wool in b1.7.3 either), no lying down, no sounds, no baby animals, hens do not flock; a rest is only standing. The chew and peck are a sine of `munch`, not an animation. UNVERIFIED: every number (durations, 1 in 70, 1 in 8, 4 blocks, gaits, angles) by eye, the look of the dipped head on a device (the pivot shift is worked out from the head box, not seen), and that it compiles (`Mob::idle` is a private method called from `ai_walk` and `roam` as their signatures read; the match guards use `rng`). `a_stray_animal_drifts_back_to_its_herd` (28 blocks in two minutes) is now slower by the pauses: if it fails, raise its 2400 ticks before touching the pauses.
 - 2026-10-25 (4): smart animals: path-walked wandering, a herd's pull and running from a blow (NOT b1.7.3; written WITHOUT a Rust toolchain: not compiled, not run; +3 tests `mobs::tests::{a_smart_pig_never_walks_off_a_cliff, a_hit_animal_runs_from_the_blow, a_stray_animal_drifts_back_to_its_herd}`, +1 assert in `options::options_txt_round_trips`; run `cargo test --lib mobs options` first). Pig, cow, sheep and chicken only; the wolf, squid and every monster keep the b1.7.3 AI untouched.
     - Navigation: the wander cell is chosen as before (10 random cells within 6 blocks, grass 10, else -0.5) but only among cells the animal can stand in (`stand_y`: a solid floor that is not a cactus, air in its body cells, within 3 cells of its feet), and it walks there along `path::find` (the A* the chase already uses): round walls, up one-block steps, never off a drop of more than 3, through water or lava. A cell the path-finder cannot reach (of the best two) means it stays put. `Mob::chase`'s point-following became `Mob::follow`, shared by both. A pause (1 tick in 100, or the path's end) drops the path and the next walk is chosen afresh.
     - Herd: `Mobs::herd` (once per AI tick, 48 mobs at most) hands each animal its nearest mate of the same kind within 24 blocks; one more than 6 blocks off adds 4 to the weight of the cells that are more than 2 blocks nearer to it, so a stray drifts back and a herd that is together wanders freely.
